      "explanation": "<p><img src=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l5dwkfem/47060c05-0e04-4935-a1ed-79d5304396a8/3f82e1e0-ff88-11ec-9933-ef22a1309b30/file-1l5dwkfen.png?format=png\" data-orsrc=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/image/1l5dwkfem/47060c05-0e04-4935-a1ed-79d5304396a8/3f82e1e0-ff88-11ec-9933-ef22a1309b30/file-1l5dwkfen.png\" loading=\"lazy\" style=\"max-width:100%;height:auto;display:block;margin:0px auto;max-height:40vh\" alt=\"JEE Main 2022 (Online) 28th June Evening Shift Chemistry - Haloalkanes and Haloarenes Question 94 English Explanation\" srcset=\"https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/500/image/1l5dwkfem/47060c05-0e04-4935-a1ed-79d5304396a8/3f82e1e0-ff88-11ec-9933-ef22a1309b30/file-1l5dwkfen.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l5dwkfem/47060c05-0e04-4935-a1ed-79d5304396a8/3f82e1e0-ff88-11ec-9933-ef22a1309b30/file-1l5dwkfen.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l5dwkfem/47060c05-0e04-4935-a1ed-79d5304396a8/3f82e1e0-ff88-11ec-9933-ef22a1309b30/file-1l5dwkfen.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l5dwkfem/47060c05-0e04-4935-a1ed-79d5304396a8/3f82e1e0-ff88-11ec-9933-ef22a1309b30/file-1l5dwkfen.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l5dwkfem/47060c05-0e04-4935-a1ed-79d5304396a8/3f82e1e0-ff88-11ec-9933-ef22a1309b30/file-1l5dwkfen.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l5dwkfem/47060c05-0e04-4935-a1ed-79d5304396a8/3f82e1e0-ff88-11ec-9933-ef22a1309b30/file-1l5dwkfen.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>\n<p>Here only carbon 12th and 13th is not taking part in the resonance. All other carbons are taking part in resonance and lone pair of O is also taking part in the resonance.</p>\n<p>As because of resonance stability of compound increases Br will not attack to any carbon which is taking part in the resonance and decrease the stability of compound.</p>\n<p>So, Br can only attack 12th carbon or 13th carbon atom but 12th carbon is a alpha carbon and it can easily donate H<sup>+</sup> ion and add Br<sup>-</sup> ion and increase stability.</p>"
